                <pb facs="0577" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1462: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-24T20:00:00+08:00">February 24, 1932—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 24—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>268. Hankow’s February 23, 4 p.m., regarding protection of Lutheran United
                    Mission at Kwangchow, Honan. Legation has telegraphically instructed
                        Peck to make formal representations in the premises to
                    the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed><lb/>For the Minister:</closer>
            </div>
